# Prefer logger over console

Use [`src/lib/logger.ts`](src/lib/logger.ts) instead of calling `console.log` or `console.error` directly in application code.

```ts
import { logger } from "@/lib/logger.ts"

// ❌ BAD
console.error(error)
console.log("poll completed")

// ✅ GOOD
logger.error(error)
logger.info("poll completed")
```

- `logger.error` for failures / unexpected paths
- `logger.info` for informational messages
- Do not introduce new `console.*` call sites in `src/`
